---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy · Gentifi" description="How Gentifi uses the details you give when you join our list or sign up your business, and how the Gentifi connector handles your requests.">
  <Header />
  <main id="main">
    <section class="section">
      <div class="container prose">
        <span class="eyebrow">Privacy</span>
        <h1>How we use your details</h1>
        <p class="updated">Last updated 21 October 2026</p>
        <p>This covers our “Stay in touch” list (the waitlist), <a href="#signup">signing up your business</a>, and the <a href="#connector">Gentifi connector</a> you can add to your AI assistant.</p>

        <h2>What we collect</h2>
        <p>When you join the waitlist we keep your name, your email address, what you’re joining as (for example a business owner or a developer), and, if you give them, your business name and postcode area. We also note which page you signed up on and when.</p>

        <h2>Why</h2>
        <p>To tell you when Gentifi launches, to invite you to join early, and to understand which kinds of businesses and places want it first. We only email you about Gentifi. We don’t sell or share your details, and we don’t use them for advertising.</p>

        <h2>Our legal basis</h2>
        <p>Your consent, which you give by joining the list. You can withdraw it at any time.</p>

        <h2>Where it’s kept</h2>
        <p>In a Google Sheet that only the Gentifi team can open. Google stores it for us as our data processor.</p>

        <h2>How long</h2>
        <p>Until Gentifi launches in your area and for up to 12 months after, unless you ask us to delete it sooner.</p>

        <h2>Your rights</h2>
        <p>You can ask to see, correct or delete your details, or to come off the list, by emailing <a href="mailto:gentifiai@gmail.com">gentifiai@gmail.com</a>. If you’re unhappy with how we’ve handled your details, you can complain to the Information Commissioner’s Office at ico.org.uk.</p>

        <h2>Who we are</h2>
        <p>Gentifi. You can reach us at <a href="mailto:gentifiai@gmail.com">gentifiai@gmail.com</a>.</p>

        <h2 id="check">When you ask for an AI visibility check</h2>
        <p>We keep your business name, its website, your email and, if you give it, your town, in the same Google Sheet as the waitlist. We use them to check what your website tells AI and to email you the report, and we may follow up once about Gentifi. We keep them for up to 12 months, unless you ask us to delete them sooner.</p>

        <h2 id="organisers">When you ask about a market, show or high street</h2>
        <p>The <a href="/events#enquire">organiser form</a> asks for your name, email and, if you give them, your phone number, plus details of your event or organisation. We keep them in the same Google Sheet as the waitlist, use them only to talk to you about Gentifi, and keep them for up to 12 months unless you ask us to delete them sooner.</p>

        <h2 id="signup">When you sign up your business</h2>
        <p>The <a href="/join">sign-up form</a> asks for your business’s name, address, phone, website, opening hours, how you take orders and what you sell, and your own name and email.</p>
        <h3>Why</h3>
        <p>To set up your shop’s page and connection, and to contact you about it. Your business’s details, products and prices are what customers’ AI assistants will see, so they go on your public Gentifi page, but only once you’ve checked them. Your own name and email are never published.</p>
        <h3>Where it’s kept, and for how long</h3>
        <p>In the same Google Sheet as the waitlist, which only the Gentifi team can open, and on our server once your shop is live. We keep it while your shop is on Gentifi and for up to 12 months after it leaves, unless you ask us to delete it sooner. Our legal basis is taking the steps you asked for to set up your business with us.</p>

        <h2 id="connector">When you use the Gentifi connector</h2>
        <p>The <a href="/connector">Gentifi connector</a> lets your AI assistant ask shops on Gentifi what they have, and prepare reservations you confirm yourself. This is what happens to your requests.</p>
        <h3>What reaches us</h3>
        <p>Only what your AI app sends when it uses a Gentifi tool: the words you’re searching for, which shop, the items and quantities, and any collection date or note for an order. Requests come from your AI app’s servers, such as Anthropic’s or OpenAI’s, not from your device. We don’t receive your name, contact details, location or chat history from your AI app, and the connector has no sign-in.</p>
        <h3>What we do with it</h3>
        <p>We use each request only to answer it, from the shop’s own catalogue, and then discard it. We don’t store, log, sell or share your requests, use them for advertising, or build a profile of you. Our server only records errors, without what you asked.</p>
        <p>When your AI prepares an order, it gives you a link to a confirmation page. The order is carried in the link itself, so preparing one stores nothing. If you tap Confirm on that page, we keep a record of what you confirmed: a reference, the shop, the items, prices and total, any collection date, and when it was prepared and confirmed. It doesn’t include who you are, and any note you added is kept only as a scrambled code (a hash), not as text. The record lets the shop match your order to its reference and shows what was agreed.</p>
        <p>Some shops answer orders in the Telegram messaging app. For those shops, the confirmation page also asks for your name and a phone number or email, so the shop can reach you. When you tap Confirm, we pass your order and those details to the shop as a Telegram message, and show you their answer on the same page. Your name and contact details aren’t added to the record of your order. Our server holds them only in its working memory while your order is open, and forgets them once it ends: when the shop declines it, it expires or is cancelled, or the shop marks it collected or delivered. It forgets them after 7 days at most, and never saves them.</p>
        <p>We do count, for each shop and each day, how many times its page was opened, how many times AI tools asked about it, how often it came up in searches and how many orders were confirmed, so we can tell shops how Gentifi is working for them. These are numbers only: we don’t record who, from where, or what was asked.</p>
        <h3>Who else is involved</h3>
        <p>Our server is hosted by Hostinger, which processes the traffic for us. Your conversation itself is handled by your AI app’s provider under their own privacy policy. If you choose to send a reservation email or use a shop’s checkout, that goes directly to the shop and is covered by the shop’s privacy terms. For shops that answer in Telegram, the message carrying your order and details is delivered by Telegram, under Telegram’s privacy policy, and the shop receives your details just as it would from an email.</p>
        <h3>How long</h3>
        <p>We don’t keep your requests. Your name and contact details for a Telegram shop are forgotten once your order ends, and after 7 days at most; they’re never saved. While an order with a Telegram shop is open, and for 7 days at most, we keep what was ordered (never who ordered it), so the shop’s answer still reaches you if our server restarts. A record of a confirmed order is kept while the shop is on Gentifi and for up to 12 months after it leaves; it doesn’t identify you, but if you want one removed, email us its reference. You can remove the connector at any time in your AI app’s settings. Questions: <a href="mailto:gentifiai@gmail.com">gentifiai@gmail.com</a>.</p>

        <h2 id="guide">When you use the Gentifi guide</h2>
        <p>The guide is the “Ask about Gentifi” chat on this site. An AI writes its answers; please don’t type personal details into it.</p>
        <h3>What reaches us, and who else is involved</h3>
        <p>Your questions go to our server, which sends the conversation to an AI model, Claude Haiku made by Anthropic, through the AI service OpenCode, to write each answer. They process it to answer you, under their own terms. Our server is hosted by Hostinger.</p>
        <p>We also see your internet address, which we use only to limit how many questions can be asked. It’s held in our server’s working memory, scrambled with a code that changes every day, and never saved.</p>
        <h3>What we keep, and for how long</h3>
        <p>The conversation is held in our server’s working memory for two hours at most, so the guide can follow it. We keep each question, without who asked, until the next morning, when the Gentifi team gets a summary of what people asked; then it’s deleted. We keep an answer only if it might break our own rules (for example, if it mentions a price), so we can check it, and it’s deleted with the questions. Your browser keeps your conversation until you close the tab. Our legal basis is our legitimate interest in answering questions about Gentifi and improving this site.</p>
        <h3>If you choose “Message us”</h3>
        <p>We keep your name, email, business if you give it, your message and, if you tick the box, your conversation with the guide, in the same Google Sheet as the waitlist. We use them only to reply to you, and keep them for up to 12 months unless you ask us to delete them sooner.</p>

        <h2>On the rest of the site</h2>
        <p>This site doesn’t use advertising or tracking cookies. The demo pages don’t send anything you type.</p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .prose { max-width: calc(46rem + var(--gutter) * 2); display: grid; gap: 14px; }
  .prose h1 { margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .prose h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-top: 18px; }
  .prose h3 { font-size: 1.05rem; margin-top: 6px; }
  .prose p { color: var(--ink-muted); }
  .prose a { color: var(--teal); font-weight: 600; }
  .updated { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 0.85rem; }
</style>
